{"package":"Zstd","version":"0.1.0","assessment":"incomplete","packageSha256":"270ef403392aff74c105d80c605df62d680fab5b53f6f6a00566b242b60737c3","scannedAt":"2026-10-24T12:05:28.277Z","scannerVersion":"0.1.0","rulesetVersion":"0.1.0","tools":{"powerShell":"7.5.12","psscriptAnalyzer":"1.25.0","psscriptAnalyzerExpected":"1.25.0"},"packageUrl":"https://www.powershellgallery.com/packages/Zstd/0.1.0","metadata":{"title":"Zstd","description":"Zstandard (zstd) compression as PowerShell cmdlets, with libzstd 1.5.7, the reference implementation, compiled into the module. Compress-Zstd compresses files, or the bytes piped to it, each into one zstd frame that carries a content checksum, at levels 1 to 22 and on up to 256 worker threads. Expand-Zstd expands every frame of a file or of piped bytes, and refuses data that is truncated, fails its checksum or names another dictionary. New-ZstdDictionary trains a dictionary from sample files, which both other cmdlets take, and -MaxMemory bounds everything a compression or an expansion commits. Bound directly to Rust with PoWerRuSt (pwrs), Rust bindings for writing PowerShell binary modules in the spirit of PyO3: the cmdlets are the library, not a wrapper over a command line. Windows x64 and Arm64 in one module, on PowerShell 7.4 or later and Windows PowerShell 5.1, with no Visual C++ Redistributable needed. Source and issues at https://github.com/Variably-Constant/Zstd; the binding framework at https://github.com/Variably-Constant/PWRS and https://crates.io/crates/PoWerRuSt.","authors":"Mark Newton","owners":"MarkusMcNugen","projectUrl":"https://github.com/Variably-Constant/Zstd","publishedAt":"2026-09-29T13:18:32.09","updatedAt":"2026-10-23T06:20:01.217","tags":["pwrs","powershell","zstd","zstandard","compression","Windows","PSModule","PSEdition_Desktop","PSEdition_Core","PSCmdlet_Compress-Zstd","PSCommand_Compress-Zstd","PSCmdlet_Expand-Zstd","PSCommand_Expand-Zstd","PSCmdlet_New-ZstdDictionary","PSCommand_New-ZstdDictionary","PSIn